# CampusEats — Study Notes

> Quick orientation: the **real app for the test is `week3-codealong/`**. Everything below is that app unless stated otherwise. `myWeb/` (plain HTML/JS) and `week5-codealong/` (Firebase login) are covered in the last section.

## TL;DR — the 30-second summary
- **React** builds the UI from small **components** (functions that return JSX).
- Data flows **down** through **props**; changes flow **up** by calling functions the parent passed down.
- **State** = a component's memory. Changing it re-renders the screen. Made with `useState`.
- **Hooks** = functions starting with `use`. Yours are `useState` and `useEffect` (no custom hooks, no Context).
- The app fetches `/api/vendors.json`, shows vendors + menus, and keeps a **cart** in `App.jsx` state (saved to localStorage).

---

## 1. How the app starts

```
index.html            ONE page. Has <div id="root"></div>
      |
   main.jsx           finds #root -> React.render(<App/>)
      |
   App.jsx            the brain: all state + cart logic + screen switching
      |
 components/*.jsx     children: Header, Footer, VendorCard, MenuList, CartPage...
```

**App.jsx is the single source of truth** for the cart. It passes data down and receives events up.

---

## 2. Core concepts

### 2.1 JSX
HTML-looking code inside JS. `{ }` lets you drop JavaScript in.

```jsx
const name = "Izzmn";
const el = <h1>Hello {name}</h1>;
```
Rules: use `className` (not `class`) · return ONE parent element (wrap siblings in `<>...</>`) · component names start with a **capital letter**.

### 2.2 Components
A function returning JSX. Small = reusable = easy to debug.

```jsx
function Footer() {
  return <footer className="footer">
    <p>&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} CampusEats</p>
  </footer>
}
export default Footer
```

### 2.3 PROPS — data going DOWN (read-only)
Props are the inputs to a component. The parent sets them; the child can only read.

```jsx
// Parent passes:
<MenuItemCard item={item} onAddToCart={handleAddToCart} />

// Child receives (destructured):
function MenuItemCard({ item, onAddToCart }) { ... }
```

Naming pattern: **`onXxx` = a function you may call** (an action). Plain names = data.

**Every prop in the app:**

| Component | Props received | Parent |
|-----------|----------------|--------|
| `Header` | `cartCount`, `onShowMenu`, `onShowCart` | App |
| `Footer` | *(none)* | — |
| `VendorCard` | `vendor`, `isSelected`, `onSelect` | App |
| `MenuList` | `items`, `onAddToCart` | App |
| `MenuItemCard` | `item`, `onAddToCart` | MenuList |
| `CartPage` | `cart`, `onChangeQty`, `onRemove`, `onPlaceOrder` | App |
| `CartItem` | `line`, `onChangeQty`, `onRemove` | CartPage |
| `CheckoutForm` | `onPlaceOrder` | CartPage |

### 2.4 STATE — the component's memory
Data that can change; changing it re-renders the component.

```jsx
const [cart, setCart] = useState([])
//     value  setter
```
- Only change it with the **setter** (`setCart(...)`). Never `cart.push(...)`.
- `setCart(prev => ...)` is the **updater form** — safest when the new value depends on the old one.

**Every piece of state in App.jsx:**

| State | Start | Controls |
|-------|-------|----------|
| `view` | `'menu'` | which screen: `'menu'` / `'cart'` / `'done'` |
| `cart` | `[]` (from localStorage) | the shopping cart |
| `cartItems` | `[]` (from localStorage) | ⚠️ duplicate + unused (see BUG-2) |
| `maxSpice` | `3` | spice-level filter slider |
| `vendors` | `[]` | all vendors from JSON |
| `selectedVendor` | `null` | currently chosen vendor |
| `loading` | `false` | show "Loading..."? |
| `error` | `null` | show error + Retry? |
| `reloadKey` | `0` | bump to re-run the fetch |

### 2.5 HOOKS — what they are
Functions that start with **`use`**. They let a component plug into React features.

**Two golden rules:**
1. Call them only at the **top level** of a component — never inside `if`, a loop, or a nested function.
2. Call them only in **React components** (or custom hooks), not plain functions.

**Hooks used in YOUR repo:**

| Hook | Where | Does |
|------|-------|------|
| `useState` | App.jsx, CheckoutForm.jsx, SearchList.jsx, Posts.jsx, week5 App.jsx | stores changing data |
| `useEffect` | App.jsx (x2), Posts.jsx, week5 App.jsx | side effects: fetch, save, subscribe |

> ❗ **No custom hooks** are defined anywhere in the repo, and there is **no cart Context** — the cart is passed by **props**. If a question assumes otherwise, the real answer is "not used".

---

## 3. useEffect in depth (side effects)

Runs **after** React paints the screen. Use it for things *outside* React: fetching, saving, timers, subscriptions.

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  // do the side effect
  return () => { /* optional cleanup */ }
}, [deps])
```

**Dependency array — the #1 exam topic:**

| deps | When it runs |
|------|--------------|
| `[]` | once, after the first render |
| `[cart]` | first render + every time `cart` changes |
| *omitted* | after EVERY render (rarely wanted) |

**The 5 effects in the repo:**

**(1) Fetch vendors — App.jsx** (re-runs when `reloadKey` changes)
```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  setLoading(true)
  fetch('/api/vendors.json')
    .then((res) => { if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch vendors'); return res.json() })
    .then((data) => {
      setVendors(data)
      if (data && data.length > 0) setSelectedVendor(data[0])   // auto-select first vendor
      setLoading(false)
    })
    .catch((err) => { setError(err.message); setLoading(false) })
}, [reloadKey])
```

**(2) Save cart — App.jsx** (runs whenever `cart` changes)
```jsx
useEffect(() => { localStorage.setItem('cart', JSON.stringify(cart)) }, [cart])
```

**(3) Save cartItems** — the same idea under key `'cartItems'` (dead code, see BUG-2).

**(4) Fetch posts + cleanup — Posts.jsx**
```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController()
  fetch(URL, { signal: controller.signal })
    .then((res) => { if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`); return res.json() })
    .then(setPosts)
    .catch((err) => { if (err.name !== 'AbortError') setError(err.message) })
    .finally(() => { if (!controller.signal.aborted) setLoading(false) })
  return () => controller.abort()   // CLEANUP: cancel fetch if component unmounts
}, [])
```

**(5) Auth listener — week5 App.jsx**
```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const unsubscribe = onAuthStateChanged(auth, setUser)
  return unsubscribe   // stop listening on unmount
}, [])
```

---

## 4. Derived values (compute, do NOT store!) & handlers

### 4.1 Derived values
If a value can be **calculated** from existing data, calculate it each render — storing it risks going out of sync.

**Cart count (the header badge) — App.jsx:**
```jsx
const cartCount = cart.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.qty, 0)
```

**Spice filter — App.jsx:**
```jsx
const menuItems = selectedVendor?.menu || []              // ?. = safe read, || [] fallback
const filteredMenu = menuItems.filter((item) => {
  const itemSpice = item.spiceLevel || 0                  // missing spice counts as 0
  return itemSpice <= maxSpice
})
```

**Cart total — CartPage.jsx (currently NOT implemented — BUG-3):**
```jsx
const total = cart.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.item.price * line.qty, 0)
```

### 4.2 Event handlers — the 4 cart functions (App.jsx)

**Add to cart** (new line, or +1 if already there):
```jsx
function handleAddToCart(item) {
  setCart((prevCart) => {
    const existing = prevCart.find((line) => line.item.id === item.id)
    if (existing) {
      return prevCart.map((line) =>
        line.item.id === item.id ? { ...line, qty: line.qty + 1 } : line)
    }
    return [...prevCart, { item, qty: 1 }]      // NEW array, never mutate
  })
}
```

**Change quantity** (+/- buttons):
```jsx
function handleChangeQty(itemId, delta) {
  setCart((prevCart) =>
    prevCart
      .map((line) => {
        if (line.item.id === itemId) {
          const newQty = line.qty + delta
          return newQty > 0 ? { ...line, qty: newQty } : null   // 0 -> drop
        }
        return line
      })
      .filter(Boolean)        // remove the nulls
  )
}
```

**Remove:**
```jsx
function handleRemove(itemId) {
  setCart((prevCart) => prevCart.filter((line) => line.item.id !== itemId))
}
```

**Place order (has a bug — see BUG-1):**
```jsx
function handlePlaceOrder(details) {
  const total = cart.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.item.price * line.qty, 0)
  setLastOrder({ ...details, total })   // ⚠️ setLastOrder/lastOrder never declared
  setCart([])
  setView('done')
}
```

---

## 5. Rendering: lists, conditionals, JSON

### 5.1 Lists with .map()
```jsx
// MenuList.jsx
function MenuList({ items, onAddToCart }) {
  if (!items || items.length === 0) return <p>No items on this menu yet.</p>
  return (
    <div className="menu-list">
      {items.map((item) => (
        <MenuItemCard key={item.id} item={item} onAddToCart={onAddToCart} />
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}
```
- `.map()` turns data into JSX.
- **`key={item.id}` is required** — React uses it to track items.
- The top guard handles the empty state.

### 5.2 Conditional rendering — 3 ways used here
```jsx
// (a) &&  — show only when true
{selectedVendor && <VendorCard vendor={selectedVendor} />}

// (b) ternary ? :  — pick between two
{item.available === false ? 'Out of stock' : 'Add to cart'}

// (c) early return  — bail out with other UI
if (!vendor) return null
if (cart.length === 0) return <p>Your cart is empty...</p>
```

**The screen switcher (App.jsx):**
```jsx
let content
if (view === 'cart')       content = <CartPage ... />
else if (view === 'done')  content = <div>Order placed...</div>
else if (loading)          content = <p>Loading...</p>
else if (error)            content = <div>{error}<button>Retry</button></div>
else                       content = <>...vendors, slider, VendorCard, MenuList...</>
// then:  <main>{content}</main>
```

### 5.3 The data file — public/api/vendors.json
Lives in `public/`, so it's served at the URL **`/api/vendors.json`**.

Shape (top level = array of vendors):
```json
[
  {
    "id": "2416264-cake-izzmn",
    "name": "Cake Izzmn",
    "location": "Mahallah Maryam, Block D",
    "openHours": "8:00 am - 11:00 pm",
    "isOpen": true,
    "menu": [
      { "id": "2416264-m1", "name": "Chocolate Cake", "price": 6.0, "category": "Desserts", "popular": true }
    ]
  }
]
```
- 3 vendors: **Cake Izzmn**, **Kafe Mahallah Siddiq**, **Makan Pagi**.
- Menu items have `id`, `name`, `description`, `price`, `category`, plus optional `spiceLevel`, `available`, `popular`.
- Student IDs are baked into the ids (`2416264-...`) — the assignment marks work that way.
- Flow: `fetch` -> `res.json()` -> `vendors` state -> auto-select `data[0]` -> passed as props.

